# Anansi Team Conventions

## Tech Stack
- Python 3.11+
- uv for dependency management
- LangGraph for agent control
- Streamlit for UI
- FastMCP for cultural context integration
- FLUX (Replicate/SiliconFlow) for images
- Google Cloud TTS for audio
- Langfuse for observability

## Architecture Rules
- Use typed interfaces (Pydantic, TypedDict) at all node boundaries.
- No loose strings passed between nodes.
- Do not implement any business logic in the view layer.
- Ensure all states in the graph are clear and observable.

## Code Style
- Use Ruff for linting and formatting (line-length 88, py311 target).
- Use Mypy in strict mode for type checking.
- Document every file, class, and function.

## What NEVER to do
- No `pip install` commands. Always use `uv`.
- No `os.getenv` in business logic — use Pydantic BaseSettings in `config.py`.
- No bare `except Exception:` blocks; always catch specific exceptions.
- No direct JSON reads in tools; encapsulate data reads within the context repository.
